---
title: CMN — Password Reset Token State Machine
---
stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> Pending : RequestPasswordRecoveryAsync()\nGenerate UUID rawToken\nEncrypt → store in Redis\nKey: PasswordReset:{rawToken}\nIsUsed = false\nTTL = 24h

    Pending : Pending\n(IsUsed = false, within TTL)

    Used : Used\n(IsUsed = true)

    Expired : Expired\n(past ExpiredTime OR Redis TTL eviction)

    Pending --> Used : ResetPasswordAsync() success\nPassword changed\nRedis entry IsUsed = true

    Pending --> Expired : 24h TTL elapsed\n(Redis auto-evict OR\nExpiredTime < now check)

    Used --> [*] : Terminal — cannot be reused\nThrows: token already used

    Expired --> [*] : Terminal — attempt throws\nThrows: token expired

    note right of Pending
        Token format: UUID (raw) stored in Redis
        URL-encoded encrypted form sent in email
        Frontend reads ?token= from URL query param
        Decrypt → Redis lookup
    end note

    note right of Used
        ResetPasswordAsync marks IsUsed = true
        before publishing PasswordResetSuccessEvent
    end note

    note right of Expired
        Checked by: ExpiredTime > DateTime.Now
        Also auto-evicted by Redis TTL (24h)
        Both paths throw UserFriendlyException
    end note
